<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lithuanian–Soviet War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1919</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-wars-of-independence">Lithuanian Wars of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lithuanian–Soviet War was fought between newly independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> from December 1918, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> advanced westwards after the German withdrawal and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>. Lithuanian volunteers, helped by German volunteer units, halted the advance and drove the Soviets back in 1919. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-lithuanian-peace-treaty">Soviet–Lithuanian Peace Treaty</a> of 1920 recognised Lithuanian independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lithuanian-soviet-war.jpg" alt="Lithuanian–Soviet War" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soviet_POWs_in_Lithuania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
